{"id": "wwdc2019-260", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/260", "wordCount": 2677, "segments": [{"start": 11.0, "text": "Hi. I'm Jacob."}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "I'm here to tell you about the"}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "Semantic Segmentation Mattes."}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "So, first, I'm going to go"}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "through what are these new types"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "of mattes."}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "And then, David is going to talk"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "you through how to leverage a"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "core image to work with these"}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "new mattes."}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "So, remember in iOS 12, we"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "introduced the Portrait Effect"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "Matte? So, this was a matte designed"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "explicitly to provide effects"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "for portraits."}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "So, we use it internally to"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "render beautiful looking"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "portrait mode photos and"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "portrait lighting photos."}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "So, in taking a closer look at"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "the Portrait effect in matte,"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "you can see how that clearly"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "delineates the foreground"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "subject from the background."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "So, this is beautifully"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "represented here as a black and,"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "black and white matte."}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "So, values of 1 indicating"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "foreground and values of zero"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "indicating background."}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "In iOS 13, we are taking this a"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "step further with Semantic"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "Segmentation Mattes."}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "So, we're introducing hair,"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "skin,"}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "and teeth."}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "So, taking a closer look at the"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "hair matte, for instance, you"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "can see how this is beautifully"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "separating the hair region from"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "the non-hair regions."}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "So, we get great hair details"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "against the background."}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "And we get great separation"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "between the non-hair regions"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "and-- and the hair."}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "Similarly, for the skin regions"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "where now we have alpha values"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "indicating how much of a pixel"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "is of type skin."}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "So, so an alpha value of .7, for"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "instance, would indicate that,"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "that a pixel is 70% of type"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "skin."}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "So, we hope these new three"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "types, three new types of mattes"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "will give you the creative"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "freedom to, to render some cool"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "effects and beautiful looking"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "photos."}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "So, a few things to note is that"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "the mattes are half size of the"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "original image."}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "That means they are half in each"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "dimension of the original image."}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "And that means quarter"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "resolution."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "So, another thing to remember is"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "that-- that these segmentation"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "mattes can actually overlap."}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "So, this is particularly true"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "for the Portrait Effects Matte"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "and the Skin Matte that will"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "inherently overlap."}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "So, these mattes do not come for"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "free. So, we heavily leveraged the"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "Apple Neural Engines for machine"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "learning spectral graph theory."}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "And looking a bit under the hood"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "what we do is we take the"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "original size image."}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "We feed it through the Apple"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "Neural Engine and together with"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "the original sized image, we, we"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "render these high-resolution,"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "high-quality with high"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "consistency segmentation mattes."}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "These are then ready to be"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "embedded into the HEIF or JPG"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "files as you know them, together"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "with the original sized image"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "and the Depth, as you know, from"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "iOS 11."}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "So, there are two distinct ways"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "to generate these two types of"}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "mattes."}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "So, so one is that they're"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "embedded in all Portrait Mode"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "captures."}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "So, you can grab them from those"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "files."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "Or even better, you can write"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "your won capture app and opt"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "into these mattes on capture."}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "So, if you have files with the"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "segmentation mattes in them, you"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "can work with them through Core"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "Image and Image I/O."}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "David's going to talk more about"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "that."}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "But first, I'm going to talk you"}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "through how to capture with AV"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "Foundation API."}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "There are four phases we're"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "going to go through here that"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "relates to the extension."}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "So, first, is when we set up the"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "AVCapturePhotoOutput."}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "So, again, is when the capture"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "request is being initiated and"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "any point in the lifecycle of"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "your app."}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "Then, two of the callbacks."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "So, one is when the settings are"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "resolved for your capture."}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "And the final one is the when"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "the Photo did finish processing."}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "So, for, for full details on"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "this, please, refer to Brad's"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "2017 talk on this exact topic."}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "Let's go through how to set up"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "AVCapturePhotoOutput."}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "So, this usually happens when"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "you're, you're setting, you're"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "configuring your session."}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "So, you've already at this point"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "on session dot begin"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "configuration, you've set your"}, {"start": 241.0, "text": "presets."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "You've added your device inputs,"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "you add your"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "AVCapturePhotoOutput."}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "At this point is when you, when"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "you tell the API what superset"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "of segmentation mattes are you"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "going to ask for at any point in"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "the lifecycle of your app."}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "When you actually want to"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "initiate your capture request,"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "you need to specify the"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "AVCapturePhoto setting."}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "So, this, this is where you tell"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "the API this is what I really"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "want in this particular capture."}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "So, here again, you can specify"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "all the ones that you already"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "enabled. Or you can specify a subset, say"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "hair or skin."}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "Now, you initiate your capture"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "request."}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "So, you give it the"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "AVCapturePhoto settings and you"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "give it the delegate where you"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "want to have your callbacks."}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "So, time passes and soon after"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "you get that, get a"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "willBeginCaptureFor callback."}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "This is when, this is when the"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "API tells you, you may have"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "asked for something but this is"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "what you're actually going to"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "get. So, this is important for the"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "Portrait Effects Matte and the"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "Semantic Segmentation Mattes"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "because if there are no people"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "in the scene, you'll actually"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "not get a matte here."}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "So, you need to check for the"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "dimension of the-- dimensions of"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "the Semantic Segmentation"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "Mattes."}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "They'll be zero, in such case."}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "More time passes."}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "The photo did finish processing."}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "So, this is when you get your"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "AV-- AVSemanticSegmentationMatte"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "back. This is the variable matte, in"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "this case."}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "So, this new class have the same"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "type of methods and properties"}, {"start": 323.0, "text": "as you know from the Portrait"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "Effects Matte."}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "That means you can rotate"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "according to Exif data."}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "You can get your CVPixelBuffer"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "reference or you can get a"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "dictionary representation for"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "each file I/O."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "So, for a full walkthrough of"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "the lifecycle of, of how to make"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "these captures, please refer to"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "the AVCam sample app."}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "It has been updated with the"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "Semantic Segmentation Mattes and"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "will take you through all these"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "different steps."}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "I'm going to hand it over to"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "David who is going to talk about"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "the Core Image."}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "All right. Thank you very much."}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "Now that we've learned how to"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "capture images with Semantic"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "Segmentation Mattes, we get to"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "have some fun and learn how we"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "can leverage Core Image to apply"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "some fun effects."}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "Now, I'm going to have a demo"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "next."}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "But I should warn you if--"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "there's clowns in this image."}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "So, if you have any coulrophobia"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "or irrational fear of clowns,"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "you know, avert your eyes."}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "All right. So, here we have an image that"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "was captured in Portrait Mode on"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "a device."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "And what we can see in this"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "application is that we can now"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "very easily see all the"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "different Semantic Segmentation"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "Mattes that are present in this"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "file."}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "We can use the-- the traditional"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "Portrait Effects Matte or we can"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "also see the Skin Matte or we"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "can see-- the Hair Matte or the"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "Teeth Matte."}, {"start": 408.0, "text": "And it's also possible to use"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "Core Image to combine these"}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "various mattes into other"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "mattes, such as this one I've"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "synthesized by using logical"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "operations to create a matte of"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "just eyes and mouth."}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "If we go back to the main image,"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "however, we see this is a"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "picture of me in Apple Park."}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "And one of the great things you"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "could do with Semantic-- with"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "Portrait Effects Mattes is you"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "could add a background very"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "easily."}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "As you can see here, we can put"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "me in a circus tent."}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "And while that really does look"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "like a circus tent, I don't look"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "like I fit in."}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "So, now we can use some fun"}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "effects."}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "For example, we can make it look"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "like I've got some clown makeup"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "on."}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "Or if we want to go a little"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "further, we can give myself some"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "green hair."}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "And lastly, we can use some of"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "these other mattes to give"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "myself some makeup."}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "So, that's what I'd like to talk"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "to you about today, is how we"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "can do these kinds of fun"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "effects in your application."}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "All right. So, most of the clown references"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "are gone now so it's safe to"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "look back."}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "All right."}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "So, we're going to be talking about three things today."}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "One is how you create matte"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "images using Core Image, how you"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "can apply filters to those"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "images, and lastly, how you can"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "save these into files."}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "So, firstly, let's talk about"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "creating matte images using Core"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "Image."}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "There are two ways."}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "One if you can create matte"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "images by using the"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "AVCapturePhoto APIs."}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "And then, from that, you can"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "create a Core Image."}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "So, the code for this is very"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "simple. What we're going to be doing is"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "using the Semantic Segmentation"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "Matte API and specifying that we"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "want either the hair or the skin"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "or the teeth."}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "And that returns an"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "AVSemanticSegmentationMatte"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "object."}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "And from that, it's trivial to"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "create a CIImage or we can just"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "substantiate a CIImage from that"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "object."}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "The other common way you're"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "going to want to create matte"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "images is by loading them from a"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "HEIF or a JPG file."}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "These files have a main image"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "which you're familiar with, a"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "typical RGB image."}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "But they also have auxiliary"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "images such as the Portrait"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "Effects Matte as well as the new"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "mattes that we're talking about,"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "the Skin Segmentation Matte and"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "the Hair and the Teeth."}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "The code for this is very"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "simple."}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "The traditional code to create a"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "CIImage from a HEIF file is just"}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "to say CIImage and specify a"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "URL. To create these auxiliary"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "images, all you do is make the"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "same call and provide an options"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "dictionary specifying which"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "matte image you want to return."}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "So, we can specify the"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "auxiliarySegmentationHairMatte."}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "Or if we want, we can get the"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "mattes for the other Semantic"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "Segmentations."}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "So, very simple."}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "Just couple lines of code."}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "The next thing we want to do is"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "talk about how you can apply"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "effects to these images."}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "So, I showed a bunch of effects."}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "I'm going to talk about one in a"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "little bit of detail."}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "What we're going to do is we're"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "going to start with a base RGB"}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "image."}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "And then, we're going to apply"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "some effect to that."}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "Let's say we want to do the"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "washed-out clown white makeup."}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "So, I'm going to apply some"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "adjustments to that."}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "Those adjustments, however,"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "apply to the entire image so we"}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "want those to be limited to just"}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "the skin area."}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "So, we're going to use the Skin"}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "Matte and then, we're going to"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "combine these three images to"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "produce the result we want."}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "Let me walk you through the code"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "for it because it's actually"}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "quite simple."}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "But first, I want to talk about"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "the top feature request we've"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "had for Core Image which is to"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "make it easier for people to"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "discover and use the 200 plus"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "built-in filters we have."}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "And that is the new header"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "called Core mage"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "CIFilterBuiltins."}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "And these allow you to use all"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "of the built-in filters without"}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "having to remember the names of"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "the filters for the names of the"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "input."}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "So."}, {"start": 645.0, "text": "It's-- it's really great."}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "So, let me show you some code"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "that will use this new header."}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "So, the first thing we're going"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "to do is create the base image."}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "And we're just going to call it image with contents of URL."}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "And that will produce the"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "traditional RGB image."}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "Now, we're going to start"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "applying some effects."}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "So, the first thing I want to do"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "is I'm going to convert it to"}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "grayscale and I'm going to use a"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "filter called the"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "maximumComponent."}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "And I'm going to give that"}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "filter an input image of the"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "base image."}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "And then, I'm going to ask for"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "that filter's output."}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "And that produces the image that"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "looks grayscale like this."}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "This doesn't look quite bright"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "enough to look like clown"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "makeup. So, we're going to apply an"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "additional filter."}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "We're going to say use the gamma"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "adjustment filter."}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "And the input to this will be"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "the previous filter's output."}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "And then, we're going to specify"}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "the power for the gamma function"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "and ask for the output image."}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "And you'll notice it's now very"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "easy to specify the power for"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "the gamma filter."}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "It's a Float rather than having"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "to remember to use NSNumber."}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "So, that's the first part of our"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "effect."}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "The next thing we want to do is"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "start by getting this Skin"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "Segmentation Matte."}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "So, again, as I described"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "earlier, we're going to start"}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "with the URL to specify that we"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "want the Skin Matte."}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "However, when we get this image,"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "notice it's smaller than the"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "other image. As we mentioned before, these"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "are half size by default."}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "So, we need to scale it up to"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "match the image, main image"}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "size."}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "So, we're going to create a"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "CGAffineTransform that scales"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "from the matte's size to the"}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "base image size."}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "And then, we're going to apply a"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "transform to the image."}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "And that produces a new image"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "which, as you expect, matches"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "the correct size."}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "The next step we're going to do"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "is start combining these two."}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "And we're going to use the"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "blendWithMask filter."}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "And this is great and we use"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "this throughout the sample I"}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "just showed."}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "We're going to specify the"}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "background image to be the base"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "RGB image which looks like this."}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "Next, we're going to specify the"}, {"start": 764.0, "text": "input image which will be the"}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "foreground image which is the"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "image which has the-- the white"}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "makeup applied."}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "And lastly, we're going to"}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "specify a mask image which is"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "the image that I showed"}, {"start": 778.0, "text": "previously."}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "Given these three inputs, you"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "can ask the blend filter for its"}, {"start": 782.0, "text": "output and the result looks like"}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "this."}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "Now, as you can see, this is"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "just the starting point. You can combine all sort of"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "interesting effects to produce"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "great results in your application."}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "Once you're done applying these"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "effects, you want to save them."}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "And, most typically, you want to"}, {"start": 798.0, "text": "save them as a HEIF or a JPG"}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "file which supports saving"}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "auxiliary images, as well."}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "So, in addition to the main"}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "image, you can also store the"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "Semantic Segmentation Mattes so"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "that either your application or"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "other applications can apply"}, {"start": 813.0, "text": "additional effects."}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "The code for this is very"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "simple. You use the Core Image API"}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "writeHEIFRepresentation."}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "And typically, you specify the"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "main image, the URL that you"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "want to save it to, and then the"}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "pixel format that you want it to"}, {"start": 829.0, "text": "be saved as, and the colorSpace"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "you want it to be saved as."}, {"start": 833.0, "text": "And what I want to highlight"}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "today is another set of options"}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "that you can provide when you're"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "saving the image."}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "So, for example, you can specify"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "the key"}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "semanticSegmentationSkinMatte"}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "and specify the skinImage or the"}, {"start": 845.0, "text": "hairImage or the teethImage."}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "And all four of these images"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "will be saved into the resulting"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "HEIF or JPG file."}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "Now, there's an alternate way of"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "getting this result, which is,"}, {"start": 856.0, "text": "if you want, you can save the"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "main images and specify the"}, {"start": 860.0, "text": "segmentation mattes as"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "AVSemanticSegmentationMatte"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "objects."}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "This again, the API is very"}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "simple. You specify the-- the URL, the"}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "primary image, the pixel format,"}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "and the color space."}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "In this case, if you want to"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "specify these objects to be"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "saved in the file, you just say"}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "AVSemanticSegmentationMattes and"}, {"start": 879.0, "text": "you provide an array of mattes."}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "So, that's what you can do using"}, {"start": 885.0, "text": "Core Image with these mattes."}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "What I talked about today is how"}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "to create images for-- for"}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "mattes, how to apply filters,"}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "and how to save them."}, {"start": 893.0, "text": "I will, however, mention that"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "the sample app I showed you has"}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "been written as a Photos App"}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "plug-in."}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "And if you want to learn about"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "how you can do that in your"}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "application so that you can save"}, {"start": 903.0, "text": "these images, not just to HEIFs"}, {"start": 904.0, "text": "but, also, into the user's Photo"}, {"start": 906.0, "text": "library, I recommend you consult"}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "these earlier presentations."}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "Especially, the \"Introduction to"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "the Photos Frameworks\" from WWDC"}, {"start": 913.0, "text": "in 2014."}, {"start": 916.0, "text": "All right."}, {"start": 917.0, "text": "And thank you all, very much, I"}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "really look forward to seeing"}, {"start": 919.0, "text": "what you do with these great"}, {"start": 920.0, "text": "features."}]}